<!-- ============ TOOL 1: 3D Mesh Tools ============ -->
<section id="mesh-tools" class="border-y border-base-content/10 bg-base-200 py-20">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <div class="mb-12 max-w-3xl">
      <span class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">Tool 1</span>
      <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl after:mt-3 after:block after:h-0.5 after:w-12 after:bg-primary after:content-['']">3D Mesh Tools</h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-xl opacity-80">Align and modify STL files from 3D scans. Scans rarely come out clean, watertight or square to anything — fix that in a few clicks, then save an STL that drops straight into CAD, a slicer or a reverse-engineering workflow.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-16 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-box border border-base-content/10 bg-base-content/10 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="bg-base-100 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold">Level on any face</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 opacity-80">Pick three points or let it find the largest flat area. Refine the fit by least squares, and flatten a rippled face perfectly flat.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-base-100 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold">Square, scale &amp; centre</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 opacity-80">Align an edge to X or Y, scale to a known dimension, and put the origin exactly where you want it — even at the centre of a hole.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-base-100 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold">Check &amp; repair</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 opacity-80">One-click health report: holes, loose pieces, non-manifold edges and flipped triangles, labelled on the model. Remove debris and fill small holes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-base-100 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold">Shrink huge scans</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 opacity-80">Type the file size you want. A 238&nbsp;MB scan becomes 20&nbsp;MB with the surface moved by thousandths of a millimetre.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-base-100 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold">Measure</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 opacity-80">Distances, angles, and the diameter and centre of any hole from three picked points.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-base-100 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold">Undo &amp; re-use</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 opacity-80">Every step is undoable and your original is never touched. The 4×4 matrix is saved so you can apply the same move to the full-resolution scan.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-6 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
